description:
In lichen/subsys/lichen/rpl/routing.c:461-462, lichen_rpl_dao_manager_build_dao_with_lifetime unconditionally increments dm->dao_sequence and dm->path_sequence BEFORE calling build_dao (line 463). If build_dao returns ERR_BUF_SMALL (buffer too small), the sequences have already been advanced.

The test at lichen/tests/rpl_routing/src/main.c:311-315 asserts:
  zassert_equal(tx_manager.dao_sequence, dao_sequence, "failed update changed DAOSequence");
  zassert_equal(tx_manager.path_sequence, path_sequence, "failed update changed Path Sequence");

This test WILL FAIL because the sequences are unconditionally incremented before build_dao can reject the short buffer.

Fix: move the sequence increments to after build_dao succeeds (inside the  block on success).
